<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Khedivate of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">1867 CE – 1914 CE · capital Cairo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Egypt under the khedives, which opened the Suez Canal, fell into debt and came under British occupation in 1882 while remaining nominally Ottoman.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1867 the Ottoman sultan granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isma-il-pasha">Ismail Pasha</a>, grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-of-egypt">Muhammad Ali</a>, the title of khedive and greater autonomy, transforming <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/egypt-under-muhammad-ali">Egypt under Muhammad Ali</a> into the Khedivate. Ismail aimed to make <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, rebuilding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> on Parisian lines.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-canal">Suez Canal</a> opened in 1869, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> boom funded railways and schools, but borrowing became ruinous. Ismail sold his canal shares to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> in 1875 and accepted Anglo-French financial control before being deposed in 1879. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmed-urabi">Ahmed Urabi's</a> nationalist revolt led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to invade in 1882, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evelyn-baring-1st-earl-of-cromer">Lord Cromer</a> effectively governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from 1883 to 1907.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> in 1914, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-ii-of-egypt">Khedive Abbas II</a>, ended Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> and declared a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>, creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-egypt">Sultanate of Egypt</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-kamel-of-egypt">Hussein Kamel</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/khedivate-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Khedivate of Egypt" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Converted to svg by Daniel78 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Egypt_(1882%E2%80%931922).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1867 CE – 1914 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cairo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ismail Pasha, Tewfik Pasha, Abbas II Hilmi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a>, <a href="/countries/sudan">Sudan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Khedivate, Egypt (Khedivate)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1890&amp;focus=khedivate-of-egypt" aria-label="Khedivate of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5491 1081 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Khedivate of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5811 1337L5811 1337M5811 1337L5709 970M5811 1337L4997 651M5811 1337L5811 1337M5811 1337L5888 1853M5811 1337L5888 1853M5811 1337L6076 1854M5811 1337L6163 2086"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5811 1337h0M5709 970h0M4997 651h0M5811 1337h0M5888 1853h0M5888 1853h0M6076 1854h0M6163 2086h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5811 1337h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5811 1337h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cairo. <a href="/atlas?year=1890&amp;focus=khedivate-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
